WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.737
-My first guest is an Oscar,
Emmy, and Golden Globe winner,

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:05.305
starring in the new movie
"Locked Down,"

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:08.474
which premieres this Thursday
on HBO Max.

00:00:08.474 --> 00:00:10.176
Here is Anne Hathaway!

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:12.011
Oh, that's what
I'm talking about.

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:13.946
Anne, welcome back to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:13.946 --> 00:00:15.181
You look fantastic.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:17.583
Thank you so much
for coming on the show.

00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:19.952
-Thank you so much.
I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:21.787
-I've known you for
a pretty long time now.

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:23.256
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:26.259
-I've heard people call you
Annie, like, your good friends.

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:29.162
Do I call you Anne or Annie?

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.596
-Call me Annie.
-Yeah.

00:00:30.596 --> 00:00:33.098
-Everybody. Everybody,
call me Annie, please.

00:00:33.098 --> 00:00:35.835
It's -- Can we talk about my
name for a second?

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:37.370
-Yeah, of course. I'd love to.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:41.774
-Okay. Can we -- Can we really
get -- Let's spill the tea.

00:00:41.774 --> 00:00:45.678
So, I -- You know,
when I was 14 years old,

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:49.282
I did a commercial
and I had to get my SAG card.

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:51.684
And they asked me, "What do you
want your name to be?"

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:52.885
And I'm like,
"Well, it should be my name.

00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:54.119
My name is Anne Hathaway."

00:00:54.119 --> 00:00:57.056
Like -- And I never --
And so that seemed like

00:00:57.056 --> 00:00:59.091
the right choice,
but it never occurred to me

00:00:59.091 --> 00:01:02.528
that, for the rest of my life,
people would call me Anne.

00:01:02.528 --> 00:01:04.864
The only person who ever calls
me Anne is my mother,

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.133
and she only does it
when she's really mad at me.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.468
Like, really mad.
-Yeah, I know that.

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:11.537
-And so every time, like,
I step out in public

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:12.638
and someone calls my name,

00:01:12.638 --> 00:01:14.073
I think they're going to
yell at me.

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:17.009
-Yeah. My mom would say
my middle name.

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:18.778
"James Thomas!"

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:22.715
-So, is -- But I doubt people
are just like, "James Thomas!

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.851
How are you?
Loved your last film."

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:26.352
People are like, "Anne."
I'm like, "What? What did I do?"

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:27.553
-"No, I'm Annie!"

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:30.589
-And so, please, seriously,
just feel free.

00:01:30.589 --> 00:01:32.692
It's not --
People are so lovely.

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:34.894
They don't want
to be presumptuous.

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:37.330
And so they come up
with workarounds on set

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:39.565
because the truth is,
nobody is comfortable

00:01:39.565 --> 00:01:41.267
calling me Anne ever.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.102
It doesn't fit. I'm an Annie.

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:44.837
And so people
call me, like, "Miss H."

00:01:44.837 --> 00:01:46.172
People call me "Hath."

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:49.676
So feel free,
call me anything but Anne.

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:52.211
-Well, Annie, congrats,
by the way.

00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:53.679
Since the last time
you were here,

00:01:53.679 --> 00:01:55.081
you had another baby.

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:57.884
You have two
beautiful boys right now.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:02:00.652
Congratulations.
How old are they?

00:02:00.652 --> 00:02:03.088
-They're 4 and they're 1.

00:02:03.088 --> 00:02:07.693
-Oh, my gosh. During quarantine?
Has it been crazy?

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:10.629
Just perfect.
-What hasn't been crazy?

00:02:10.629 --> 00:02:13.333
Like, yes, like, on the list of
things that are crazy --

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:14.801
It's been a lot.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:19.339
But, I mean, those are good ages
to be home with your kids,

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:21.507
because, you know,
our 4-year-old believes

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:23.042
everything we tell him.

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:27.346
And that's adorable,
as well as very useful.

00:02:27.346 --> 00:02:29.815
And our 1-year-old
is just, like --

00:02:29.815 --> 00:02:31.483
It's just the most magic age.

00:02:31.483 --> 00:02:32.785
You know, we've just been home
with him since he was

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.987
4 months old,
just with him every single day,

00:02:34.987 --> 00:02:37.056
and that's been a gift.

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:38.124
-Yeah, that's pretty wild.

00:02:38.124 --> 00:02:40.192
-But the 4-year-old --
Did you, like,

00:02:40.192 --> 00:02:42.327
tell your kids everything
when they were 4, like,

00:02:42.327 --> 00:02:44.396
to kind of get them to do what
you wanted them to do?

00:02:44.396 --> 00:02:46.065
-Oh, yeah.
I mean, yeah, sure, whatever.

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:47.866
I still kind of do it, yeah.

00:02:47.866 --> 00:02:49.802
I'll just go, "We'll do that,
and then we'll get this."

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:53.072
But, yeah, I mean, I was --
When they were really babies,

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:55.675
I was trying to get Winnie
to say "dada" so hard,

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:56.976
to make that her first word.

00:02:56.976 --> 00:03:00.579
-We know. We know, Jimmy.
-Do I have the book around?

00:03:00.579 --> 00:03:01.814
I don't. But if I did --

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:06.219
-Well, I have the book,
and it works, darn it.

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:08.354
-Dude, I was calling
everything "dada."

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:11.090
I was calling the bottle --
-You jerk. You jerk.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:14.527
-Really? I was calling
the bottle of milk "dada."

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.128
-We should have
talked about this before

00:03:16.128 --> 00:03:18.164
so I could really
let you know how I feel.

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:20.833
-I also put out "mama."
I have "mama."

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:21.968
You got to read that book.

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.769
-You didn't send
that one to me, sweetie.

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:26.839
-Oh, you know what?
Quarantine. It's in the mail.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.641
-Oh, yeah. No, no.
Of course. I understand.

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:31.077
I have to. I have to understand.
-"I have to understand."

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:32.811
-But my 4-year-old --
it's the best,

00:03:32.811 --> 00:03:36.115
because over the holidays,
like, this was the first year

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:38.016
he's really believed
in Santa Claus.

00:03:38.016 --> 00:03:40.252
And we were driving in the car,
and you know when, like,

00:03:40.252 --> 00:03:41.720
you're in the car
with your kids,

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:43.690
and, suddenly,
the car just gets too hot?

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:44.857
-Yes.

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.693
-Like, all of a sudden,
like, in a second,

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:49.962
and everybody gets, like,
loud at the same moment.

00:03:49.962 --> 00:03:52.164
And the baby is crying
because he wants the cracker

00:03:52.164 --> 00:03:53.366
that the 4-year-old has,

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:54.901
and 4-year-old will not
give him a cracker.

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.235
-Yeah.

00:03:56.235 --> 00:03:57.970
-And, like, just won't do it,
won't do it, won't do it.

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:00.440
And then, finally,
I just have this spark

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:05.277
and I go, "Okay, Johnny,
but what about Santa?"

00:04:05.277 --> 00:04:08.280
Like, his hand shot out
straight towards me.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.148
I had the entire
box of crackers suddenly.

00:04:10.148 --> 00:04:11.484
There was no argument.

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:13.252
And Adam and I turned to each
other, and we went,

00:04:13.252 --> 00:04:15.154
"Oh, my God,
this is so powerful."

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:19.158
-Wow. What did we just -- That's
right.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:24.296
So, 4 and 1, you know, the ages
are the ages that they are,

00:04:24.296 --> 00:04:26.365
but there's a lot of
magic in those ages.

00:04:26.365 --> 00:04:29.168
-This -- You know, I tried not
to do Elf on the Shelf,

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:30.336
just 'cause I go, "I don't know.

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.972
I have enough things
to worry about, you know,

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:35.241
and to have the
Elf on the Shelf thing."

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:36.875
And you want to hear the
weirdest thing?

00:04:36.875 --> 00:04:38.744
It showed up in my house.

00:04:38.744 --> 00:04:40.212
We do it now.
-What do you mean?

00:04:40.212 --> 00:04:42.781
-The elf is in my -- Somehow --
I don't know how we got it,

00:04:42.781 --> 00:04:44.851
but the Elf on the Shelf
is now in my house,

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:46.819
and it does stuff every holiday.

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:48.121
-We had to come up
with something,

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:50.223
because, like,
Johnny would leave the room,

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:52.091
and then Jack would mess
with his stuff.

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:53.726
And Johnny would
come back and be like,

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:55.027
"Who messed with my stuff?"

00:04:55.027 --> 00:04:57.430
And we came up with
the demolition elves.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:59.932
-What? Oh, interesting.

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:01.534
-So at nighttime --
at nighttime,

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:02.801
after he went to bed,
the demolition elves

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:03.903
messed with his stuff.

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:05.738
There's nothing
we could do about it.

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:08.308
Like, "No, it certainly wasn't
your brother,

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:09.875
who you're now going to
whale on --

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:12.311
now you're
not going to whale on."

00:05:12.311 --> 00:05:15.081
-I want to talk about
your new movie, "Locked Down,"

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:16.249
because it's so --

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:18.217
-You're saying that very well.
-Thank you.

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:22.488
Well, I don't want say it's --
It's not "Lockdown." It's --

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:24.557
-It's not "Lockdown."
It's "Locked Down."

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:25.958
You're right -- I guess you do
have to kind of --

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:28.327
-I just wanted to make sure
people can hear the title.

00:05:28.327 --> 00:05:30.930
-Honestly, have a glass a wine
before you watch the movie,

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:31.930
it'll be "Lockdown."

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:34.667
-"Lockdown."
-"Lockdown."

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:37.203
"Babe, honey,
let's just watch it.

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:38.270
I don't care."
-Let's just watch "Lockdown."

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:40.306
I don't know. It's on HBO Max.

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:42.241
-HBO Max? Yeah, we have that.

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:43.643
-Yeah, sure.
It's one word. Who cares?

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:45.111
"Lockdown."

00:05:45.111 --> 00:05:47.613
It's a fun heist movie,

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:49.982
but, also,
there's a little love in there.

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:53.252
And funny.
I thought it was fantastic.

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:56.922
How do you describe the movie?

00:05:56.922 --> 00:06:00.392
-The story -- So, I act in it --
It's directed by Doug Liman.

00:06:00.392 --> 00:06:02.594
So if you're a fan of
Doug Liman movies,

00:06:02.594 --> 00:06:05.731
you know to expect a lot and
many different wonderful things.

00:06:05.731 --> 00:06:07.666
And I act
opposite Chiwetel Ejiofor,

00:06:07.666 --> 00:06:09.702
who is just a dream.

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:13.372
Oh, my God. He's amazing.
And wonderful in this.

00:06:13.372 --> 00:06:14.841
And he's never played
a part like this before.

00:06:14.841 --> 00:06:17.743
And we play two people in
a long-term relationship

00:06:17.743 --> 00:06:19.544
that has run its course.

00:06:19.544 --> 00:06:24.183
And the day after we have our,
like, can't-take-it-back,

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:26.919
end-it-all rager of a fight,

00:06:26.919 --> 00:06:28.721
my character gets a call
that one of my co-workers

00:06:28.721 --> 00:06:30.723
is experiencing symptoms,
and we are now to be

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:33.893
locked down with each other
for 14 days in quarantine.

00:06:33.893 --> 00:06:37.663
And we sort of lose our minds,
find each other,

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:41.233
and then somehow decide to
steal a £3 million diamond

00:06:41.233 --> 00:06:42.835
from a mass murderer.

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:46.104
-And how did you even get
Harrods to play?

00:06:46.104 --> 00:06:49.775
-So, the climax of the movie
takes place in Harrods.

00:06:49.775 --> 00:06:52.111
I don't know is the short of it.

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:54.246
I think it's this 2020 thing,

00:06:54.246 --> 00:06:59.351
because Doug and Steven
had 40 pages that they said,

00:06:59.351 --> 00:07:03.055
"We've got 40 pages, an idea,
but if you don't say yes

00:07:03.055 --> 00:07:05.591
to our needing to shoot
the finale of the movie

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:08.994
in your store, there's no point
in us making it.

00:07:08.994 --> 00:07:10.929
So can we get
a 'yes' or a 'no'?"

00:07:10.929 --> 00:07:12.565
And Harrods said yes.

00:07:12.565 --> 00:07:13.732
And you would
expect them to be like,

00:07:13.732 --> 00:07:15.268
"We have to call our lawyers.

00:07:15.268 --> 00:07:16.702
We have to run it through this.
We have to do market research."

00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:18.538
But it was 2020, and they were
like, "You know what?

00:07:18.538 --> 00:07:19.938
Why not?"

00:07:19.938 --> 00:07:23.242
-It's legendary. It's Harrods.
Come on.

00:07:23.242 --> 00:07:24.309
Anyways, I want to show a clip.

00:07:24.309 --> 00:07:26.645
Here is Anne Hathaway in
"Locked Down."

00:07:26.645 --> 00:07:28.948
Take a look at this.

00:07:28.948 --> 00:07:34.219
-£3 million, tax-free,
no consequences.

00:07:34.219 --> 00:07:35.921
-One for me, one for you,
one for the NHS.

00:07:35.921 --> 00:07:36.989
-You have thought about this.

00:07:36.989 --> 00:07:39.124
-You know,
I need to go meditate.

00:07:39.124 --> 00:07:42.361
-Well, are you sure they won't
check it in New York?

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:43.729
-Shut up! I need to meditate.

00:07:43.729 --> 00:07:46.498
-No, what were you gonna say?

00:07:46.498 --> 00:07:48.267
-The man who bought
the diamond is bad.

00:07:48.267 --> 00:07:50.169
He's really bad,
and you and I are good.

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:52.437
And the NHS is good,
and good is better than bad.

00:07:52.437 --> 00:07:53.639
And when I explained
all that to grandma,

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:55.474
even she said,
"Well, yeah, that's true."

00:07:55.474 --> 00:07:58.144
And she was a Calvinist,
straight as a rod,

00:07:58.144 --> 00:08:02.248
unlike me, who is weak
in the face of temptation.

00:08:04.416 --> 00:08:06.485
-Live wild or die, Linda.

00:08:06.485 --> 00:08:07.753
-Anne Hathaway, everybody.

00:08:07.753 --> 00:08:10.690
"Locked Down" premieres
this Thursday on HBO Max.

